      "message": "Narrowing to `except ResourceNotFound` also lets transport errors propagate, not just 401/403/5xx. `get_request` raises `BadfishException(\"Failed to communicate with server.\")` on a connection failure or timeout, and `_find_resource` does not catch it, so it is not a `ResourceNotFound`. A transient probe blip during `list_interfaces` now hard-fails the call where it used to degrade to the Ethernet-interface fallback. Commit only names auth/server errors, so this is worth a note. `list_interfaces` also has no test coverage, so the new degrade-vs-propagate boundary is unpinned.",
